# Possible shift in "first": in P5, C2 and P6 it reads as the first member of a given ordered series of causes.
# In C it could read as a single uncaused cause of all series, the one named God.
# That gap is a matter of scope and quantifier (one first cause per series versus one for every series).
# It is not a clear change in the sense of the word, so I left "first" as one sense with no bridge.
